--- MacBook Duo / Hinge Glass ---

The glass shader in src/glassshader.h is a line-by-line port of the Metal shader
of the macOS prototype "MacBook Duo / Hinge Glass", from Swift and Metal to
GLSL, with four changes. The file header of src/glassshader.h lists them.

The prototype publishes no repository and no license file. Its author permits
modification of the code. The maintainer of this project verified that
statement. If the author later adds a license or objects, the wish of the
author applies.

--- Atomicx7/Duo-animation ---

The projection model of the original iPhone Duo folding animation.
https://github.com/Atomicx7/Duo-animation

The prototype above names this project as its own reference. It also publishes
no license file.

--- Mac Duo (Apache License 2.0) ---

Several timing and smoothing mechanisms come from Mac Duo:

    Mac Duo
    Copyright 2026 Makito
    Originally developed by Makito.
    https://github.com/sumimakito/Mac-Duo

The original NOTICE is kept above, as clause 4(d) of the Apache License 2.0
requires. The license text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The ported parts, changed from Swift and AppKit to C++ and Qt:

  * The critically damped spring. Source: Sources/MacDuo/CriticallyDampedSpring.swift
  * The "still" test, which uses a reference point and a tolerance instead of
    "no change at all". Source: Sources/MacDuo/LidController.swift, isPastTimeout
  * The minimum display time, 0.35 s. Same source.
  * Adaptive polling, at a low rate when idle and a high rate when active.
    Same source.
  * The observation that one mipmap sample can approximate the blur of many
    taps. This became the Taps setting of this project.
    Source: Sources/MacDuo/DepthShaders.swift

--- KWin (GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0-or-later) ---

This project is a KWin effect plugin. It links KWin::kwin and uses the public
effect API. The offscreen framebuffer pattern comes from the built-in effects
screentransform and zoom. The fullscreen quad and the shader loading pattern
come from screentransform. KWin uses the dual license GPL-2.0-or-later and
GPL-3.0-or-later, and it permits the upgrade to GPLv3.

